WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.907
- When you see a black or
latino youngster, particularly

00:00:02.907 --> 00:00:05.601
on the street, you walk to
the other side of the street.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.132
- He should be worried about
the fact that there is actual

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:10.593
thuggish behavior taking place.

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:15.593
(A mix of undistinguishable voices)

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:19.440
- The parents of black and
latino youngsters, particularly

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.358
to not let their children
go out wearing hoodies.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.011
- It's ridiculous.

00:00:28.651 --> 00:00:30.208
Everybody owns hoodies.

00:00:30.372 --> 00:00:34.807
- It's weird that I have
to like think about like

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:38.406
alright man, I'm going out to this thing.

00:00:38.406 --> 00:00:41.657
Should I be wearing a hoodie
or should I try to wear a

00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:44.652
button-up and try not to give off

00:00:44.652 --> 00:00:46.417
that vibe of danger to anyone.

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.294
- If I wore like a straight
red shirt and like red shoes,

00:00:50.294 --> 00:00:53.545
my mom would not let me go
out of the house, you know,

00:00:53.545 --> 00:00:55.960
because she thinks that I'm gonna be

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.189
perceived as a gang banger, whatever.

00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:01.439
- MLK had on a suit when
he got shot, you know.

00:01:01.439 --> 00:01:03.970
We've worn different articles
of clothing our entire lives.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.082
It doesn't make you less of a
victim cuz of what you wear.

00:01:07.082 --> 00:01:08.150
- It's different.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:11.725
For us, it's not only just for
like job interviews and stuff

00:01:11.725 --> 00:01:13.374
like that, it's going out at night, it's

00:01:13.374 --> 00:01:14.906
going to bars and stuff like that.

00:01:14.906 --> 00:01:19.906
- My style is comfortable
without looking like Steve Jobs.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:24.101
I'm not gonna walk around
wearing like a turtleneck.

00:01:24.101 --> 00:01:26.539
- First time that I was
really called a nigger,

00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:29.929
me and a few of my boys, some girls

00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:32.785
invited us down to some high school show.

00:01:32.785 --> 00:01:36.825
Now, we didn't know that she is the

00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:39.124
only black girl in this high school.

00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:41.353
So we go down to her
school to see this show,

00:01:41.353 --> 00:01:44.000
and as we're sittin' there
watchin' it, we heard somebody

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.345
yell, "Who invited the niggers?"

00:01:46.345 --> 00:01:49.340
I was like, what?

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.523
They can't be talking about
me, I'm wearing a polo.

00:01:51.523 --> 00:01:54.866
- I feel like that the
hoodie thing is an excuse,

00:01:54.866 --> 00:01:58.488
you know what I mean, it's
easier to say it's the jacket

00:01:58.488 --> 00:02:02.900
that you're wearing than the
skin color of the person.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.967
- I just started wearing
like baseball caps

00:02:04.967 --> 00:02:09.541
because if I wear it, like
I like wearing 'em low.

00:02:09.541 --> 00:02:11.839
If I wear a baseball cap low in a car,

00:02:11.839 --> 00:02:13.952
I'm gonna get pulled over easy.

00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:16.715
It's not even a question.

00:02:16.715 --> 00:02:17.617
- I've always had hoodies.

00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:18.592
I've never been told I couldn't

00:02:18.592 --> 00:02:20.310
wear one for a certain reason.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.189
I'm aware of how it may be perceived,

00:02:23.189 --> 00:02:24.861
but that's not my fault.

00:02:24.861 --> 00:02:27.462
The way that it's perceived has
nothing to do with who I am.

00:02:27.462 --> 00:02:32.115
(sad music)

